{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"fd60422dd09c955a16a103c14b6550b70814c486365a212c9f5d7533f82bd033","digest":{"component_or_area":"BindingStore baseline synchronization","key_entities":["BindingStore.set_baseline","baseline_advanced_at","binding_store.py","reconcile.py","apply_inbound_records.py","BindingStore.seed_baselines_from_snapshot","bindings.json","test_binding_baseline.py","test_reconcile_idempotency.py"],"problem_keywords":["unnecessary write","volatile timestamp","write-when-changed guard","git delta churn","binding store","baseline synchronization"],"propositions":["The baseline_advanced_at timestamp field is never read in production and can be deleted.","BindingStore.set_baseline unconditionally writes baseline and timestamp, causing pathological git delta churn across stable baseline values.","A write-when-changed guard comparing stored and new baseline values can suppress unnecessary writes and eliminate the volatile timestamp.","Integration tests must verify that two consecutive reconciler passes over unchanged Jira state produce byte-identical bindings.json and no new git commits.","Removing baseline_advanced_at from the baseline write path reduces packed repository size from 13.84 KiB/version to 2.33 KiB/version (16.8% of original)."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787613514027133001,"uuid":"893d5098-0431-4fab-a3ee-7d3392b99af7"}